What this project includes
--------------------------
Only catalogue metadata: names, years, publishers, credits, contents, hashes,
flags, download/media URLs, credits, facts and notes. It does not include disk
images, screenshots or other binary media. Media entries contain addresses and
credit lines only; the consumer fetches any picture from its source.

Generated data
--------------
The generated JSON is an adaptation of the PirateFinder catalogue and is
published under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0. Attribution and the share-alike obligation
apply. It is non-commercial. See LICENSE-DATA.

Changes made by this converter:
  - extraction into a JSON schema (disks, contents, images, media, trivia,
    links, crews, series, sources);
  - compact media address reconstruction (prefix + rest) and credit expansion;
  - optional platform filter (all, atari-st, amiga);
  - no raw SQLite database is published.

No game archive data
--------------------
This project contains no data from, and makes no reference to, any game
archive or launcher. It is a generic PirateFinder catalogue converter.
